{"t": 1795079677.8279629, "kind": "assistant", "text": "The Limit Login Attempts Reloaded plugin is incompatible with PHP 8.3 and is causing fatal errors on the front-end. I cannot deactivate it myself per the rules. To proceed with the PHP upgrade, the site owner must either:\n\n1. Replace Limit Login Attempts Reloaded with a compatible alternative (e.g., Login Lockout, Limit Login Attempts Reloaded Pro, or Wordfence)\n2. Temporarily disable the plugin during the upgrade and re-enable it after verifying compatibility\n\nUntil this plugin issue is resolved, the PHP upgrade cannot be completed. I recommend addressing this before moving forward."}
